bility)\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\tThe backend currently has a large “single-file service” shape. Before adding 50+ endpoints, split into modules.\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t- **BE-CORE-01**: Create backend module layout\\n    88\\t  - `backend/config.py` (Settings)\\n    89\\t  - `backend/db.py` (engine/session dependencies)\\n    90\\t  - `backend/security.py` (already exists)\\n    91\\t  - `backend/routers/*.py` (grouped endpoints)\\n    92\\t  - `backend/services/*.py` (business rules: xp, progression, streak, badges)\\n    93\\t  - `backend/schemas/*.py` (Pydantic DTOs)\\n    94\\t  - Update `backend/main.py` to only mount routers.\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t- **BE-CORE-02**: Add `/api/v1/health`\\n    97\\t  - Returns DB connectivity + build metadata (git sha optional).\\n    98\\t  - Used by uptime monitors and deploy checks.\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t- **BE-CORE-03**: Rate limiting strategy\\n   101\\t  - Minimum: per-IP for auth endpoints.\\n   102\\t  - Optional: API gateway or nginx `limit_req` (see deployment docs).\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t## Acceptance Criteria (Backend “Core Gameplay”)\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t1. A user can:\\n   107\\t   - list urns → open urn → list motifs → unlock motif → read lesson → complete lesson → take quiz → see XP/rank updated.\\n   108\\t2. All write endpoints are safe under retries (no duplicate XP, no duplicate progress rows).\\n   109\\t3. OpenAPI reflects all endpoints (with auth + response models).\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\t\\nTotal lines in file: 111\\n\"}\n    254\t```\n    255\t\n...\n    258\t\n    259\t```json\n>   260\t{\"output\":\"Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /root/luuniensuki-lms/docs/plan/02_Quiz_System.md:\\n     1\\t# 02_Quiz_System.md\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t## Goal\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tImplement the **quiz loop** that upgrades a motif from `discovered → learned → mastered` and awards XP/badges.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\tThis is the “core LMS” gameplay loop; without quizzes the product is only a “viewer”.\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## Current State\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t- DB models exist:\\n    12\\t  - `QuizQuestion`\\n    13\\t  - `QuizAttempt`\\n    14\\t  - `UserProgress` already has `quiz_attempts`, `quiz_best_score`, `learned_at`, `mastered_at`\\n    15\\t- Seed script currently imports some quiz questions (multiple-choice only).\\n    16\\t- **No quiz APIs** exist yet.\\n    17\\t- Frontend has no quiz pages/components.\\n    18\\t\\n    19\\t## UX Flow (Target)\\n    20\\t\\n    21\\t1. User unlocks motif in 3D → status `discovered`.\\n    22\\t2. User reads lesson → status `learned` (new endpoint).\\n    23\\t3. User takes quiz:\\n    24\\t   - pass threshold → status `mastered`\\n    25\\t   - fail → stay `learned` (or `discovered` if you allow quiz without lesson)\\n    26\\t4. XP/rank updates; optional badge awards.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t## Backend API Design\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t### 1) Fetch quiz questions\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\t- **BE-QUIZ-01**: `GET /api/v1/motifs/{motif_id}/quiz`\\n    33\\t  - Auth required (recommended). If guest support is desired, allow for demo motifs only.\\n    34\\t  - Response:\\n    35\\t    - motif metadata\\n    36\\t    - list of active questions\\n    37\\t    - for each question: **do not include `correct_answer`**\\n    38\\t  - Options should be shuffled server-side (deterministic shuffle can be added later).\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t### 2) Submit quiz attempt\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t- **BE-QUIZ-02**: `POST /api/v1/quizzes/submit`\\n    43\\t  - Auth required.\\n    44\\t  - Request includes:\\n    45\\t    - `motif_id`\\n    46\\t    - `answers`: `[{question_id, answer}]`\\n    47\\t    - `time_taken_seconds`\\n    48\\t  - Server responsibilities:\\n    49\\t    - load questions (active only)\\n    50\\t    - validate answers reference the given motif questions\\n    51\\t    - compute score + pass/fail\\n    52\\t    - insert `QuizAttempt`\\n    53\\t    - update `UserProgress`:\\n    54\\t      - increment `quiz_attempts`\\n  